==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|En-ca-did.ogg|a=CA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪd|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|do||spast}}
#: {{ux|en|Jeez, '''did''' I make a mistake!}}
#: {{ux|en|I never '''did''' like her much.}}
#: {{ux|en|What '''did''' happen when the principal found out?}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=II|canto=VI|page=254|passage=Then ſhe with liquors ſtrong his eies '''did''' ſteepe, / That nothing ſhould him haſtily awake{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1913|author={{w|Edgar Rice Burroughs}}|title={{w|The Return of Tarzan}}|publisher=Ballantine Books|location=New York|year_published=1963|page=110|passage=Monsieur Thuran became a frequent visitor at the home of Hazel Strong’s uncle in Cape Town. His attentions were very marked, but they were so punctiliously arranged to meet the girl’s every wish that she came to depend upon him more and more. '''Did''' she or her mother or a cousin require an escort—was there a little friendly service to be rendered, the genial and ubiquitous Monsieur Thuran was always available.}}
# {{lb|en|nonstandard|especially|_|Southern US|AAVE}} {{past participle of|en|do|nocat=1}}; [[done]]
#* {{quote-book|en|date=1 March 2008|author=Jody Miller|publisher=NYU Press|title=Getting Played: African American Girls, Urban Inequality, and Gendered Violence|isbn=9780748686971|page=140|url=https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=pZf9Hk-3NysC|passage={{...}}But I don't care, I mean I don't even care. She shouldn't have '''did''' that."}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2013-06-12|artist=w:Kodak Black|album=Project Baby|track=16|title=Shoulda Woulda|url=https://genius.com/Kodak-black-shoulda-woulda-lyrics|passage=I should've '''did'''{{...}}Should've turned down, now I'm really on it. Should've, could've '''did'''. Would've could've '''did'''{{...}}Ooh, I should've '''did''' em in.}}

